curator/` before implementation\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add transactional staging to research-curator file rewrites for crash-safe entry updates\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Confirm all information needed to plan and implement crash-safe atomic writes in @research-curator is available.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (atomic write staging for crash safety) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description and existing groomed sections \u2014 write-to-tmp-then-rename pattern fully specified\\n2. Scope boundaries (confined to @research-curator write operations in ./research/) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description scopes to WriteFile, UpdateEntry, FixIssues nodes in .claude/agents/research-curator.md\\n3. Existing write sites in agent file | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read .claude/agents/research-curator.md lines 40-66 \u2014 WriteFile (line 52), UpdateEntry (lines 59/62), FixIssues (lines 65-66) \u2014 all direct Write calls, no staging present\\n4. validate_research.py collect_files glob | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read validate_research.py line 369 \u2014 rglob(\\\"*.md\\\") does not match .md.tmp files; naming convention safe\\n5. Post-actions section uses direct git add (no staging) | Snapshot: not listed \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read SKILL.md lines 354-388 \u2014 post_actions block uses git add ./research/ directly, no pre-write staging\\n6. Crash scenario specifics | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description enumerates all cases (process crash, disk-full, OOM kill, network drop); write-to-tmp-then-rename handles all generically \u2014 no per-scenario branching needed\\n7. Temp file cleanup policy | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Acceptance Criterion #4 in existing groomed body specifies both outcomes (clean up OR logged warning) as acceptable \u2014 no human decision blocks planning\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Crash scenario specifics: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (item description enumerates all crash types; generic staging handles all)\\n- Temp file cleanup policy: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (AC #4 specifies both outcomes as acceptable)\\n- Post-actions section: (new) AVAILABLE (verified no staging in SKILL.md lines 354-388)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add transactional staging to research-curator file rewrites for crash-safe entry updates** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md \u2014 pattern: Crash-safe file operations via .tolaria-rename-txn/ staging directory\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Atomic write staging for crash safety in research-curator file writes |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Scoped to @research-curator file write operations in ./research/ |\\n| Existing write sites | AVAILABLE | WriteFile (line 52), UpdateEntry (line 59), FixIssues (line 62) in .claude/agents/research-curator.md \u2014 all direct writes, no staging |\\n| validate_research.py collect_files glob | AVAILABLE | rglob(\\\"*.md\\\") at lines 363-365 \u2014 .md.tmp files NOT matched; naming convention safe |\\n| Crash scenario specifics | MISSING | Which crash type (agent cancel, OS kill, disk-full) \u2014 affects error path design |\\n| Temp file cleanup policy | MISSING | Auto-clean stale .tmp files on startup vs warn-only \u2014 not specified |\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A for feature item \u2014 this is a missing safeguard, not a reproducible defect.\\n\\nObservable gap (demonstration sequence):\\n1. Run @research-curator to write or rerun a research entry\\n2. Send SIGKILL to the Claude Code process mid-write (before Write tool call completes)\\n3. Observe: ./research/{category}/{name}.md contains partial content truncated at interruption point\\n4. Run: `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py ./research/{category}/{name}.md`\\n5. Observe: validation errors due to truncated/partial content; no rollback possible\\n\\nThe absence of staging means no mechanism exists to prevent partial content from appearing at the final path.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 research-curator is used in batch/rerun mode on the full ./research/ directory. A single interruption corrupts an entry silently. The validator detects corruption after the fact but cannot restore the previous state. Risk is proportional to batch size and frequency of use. The fix is low-effort (3 Mermaid nodes to expand) making the benefit-to-effort ratio high.\\n\\nEffort: Small (3 write nodes in .claude/agents/research-curator.md Mermaid diagram to expand; validate_research.py already excludes .md.tmp at line 369 \u2014 no Python change required)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen @research-curator writes or updates ./research/{category}/{resource-name}.md:\\n1. If the write completes successfully, the entry file contains the full new content.\\n2. If the write is interrupted after writing begins but before completion, the entry file retains its previous valid content unchanged.\\n3. No entry file ever exists in a partially-written state after any operation terminates.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe research entry write uses a write-to-temp-then-rename staging pattern at all three write sites in @research-curator:\\n- New entry mode (WriteFile node): write to ./research/{category}/{name}.md.tmp, then rename to ./research/{category}/{name}.md on success.\\n- Rerun mode (UpdateEntry node): same staging pattern applied when overwriting an existing entry.\\n- Fix mode (FixIssues node): same staging pattern applied when applying targeted fixes.\\n\\nStale .tmp files from prior crashes are detectable by naming convention and cleanable independently without touching real entries.\\n\\nThe agent treats Mermaid workflow diagrams as executable procedures. The staging sequence must appear inside the workflow Mermaid diagrams at each write node \u2014 not only in prose.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After a successful new-entry write, no .md.tmp file exists alongside the entry. The entry file contains the full expected content and passes `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` with no errors.\\n2. When @research-curator is interrupted after writing the temp file but before rename completes, the original `./research/{category}/{name}.md` remains unchanged and passes validate_research.py with its prior status.\\n3. Running `collect_files()` from validate_research.py against a directory containing a .md.tmp file returns zero results for that temp file \u2014 confirmed by `rglob(\\\"*.md\\\")` at line 369 of validate_research.py not matching the `.md.tmp` extension.\\n4. A stale .md.tmp file left from a prior crash either (a) is cleaned up on the next agent run or (b) produces a logged warning \u2014 it is never silently read or merged into a valid entry.\\n5. All three write nodes in @research-curator Mermaid workflow diagram (WriteFile, UpdateEntry, FixIssues) contain the 3-step staging sequence: (1) write full content to {target}.md.tmp, (2) verify temp file written, (3) rename/move {target}.md.tmp to {target}.\\n6. Grep of `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` for `.md.tmp` returns at least three matches (one per write node).\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- What specific crash scenario prompted this item \u2014 agent cancel via Ctrl-C, Claude Code session timeout, OS kill, or disk-full?\\n- Should stale .md.tmp files be auto-cleaned on the next agent run, or only emit a warning for manual inspection?\\n- Is there an existing temp file suffix convention in this repo that should be followed for consistency?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent | .claude/agents/research-curator.md |\\n| Skill | /research-curator (SKILL.md at .claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md) |\\n| Script | .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py |\\n| Prior art | ./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md \u2014 Patterns Worth Adopting #3: crash-safe file operations via .tolaria-rename-txn/ staging |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone change to agent Mermaid workflow\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 3 Mermaid workflow nodes in .claude/agents/research-curator.md each need expanding from a single Write step into a 3-step staging sequence (write temp, verify, rename). validate_research.py already excludes .md.tmp files at line 369 \u2014 no Python change required. SKILL.md post-actions block needs no change. No new modules, no schema changes, no orchestrator changes.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` \u2014 the agent IS the interface; all three write nodes (WriteFile, UpdateEntry, FixIssues) require expanding from single Write step to 3-step staging sequence\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 no other agents read from `./research/` during write operations\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- None identified\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md::WriteFile` \u2014 Mermaid node at diagram line 52; direct Write call to `./research/category/resource-name.md`; requires staging sequence expansion\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md::UpdateEntry` \u2014 Mermaid node at diagram line 59/62; direct Write/overwrite of existing entry; requires staging sequence expansion\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md::FixIssues` \u2014 Mermaid node at diagram lines 65-66; direct Write applying targeted fixes; requires staging sequence expansion\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 no CI workflow tests research-curator write behavior\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe existing item design intent (write-to-temp-then-rename staging at three write nodes; .md.tmp naming convention; Mermaid diagram as executable procedure) is consistent with the agent's existing architecture:\\n- The agent already treats its Mermaid flowchart as an executable procedure (per SKILL.md header directive at line 11-13)\\n- validate_research.py already uses rglob(\\\"*.md\\\") at line 369 which inherently excludes .md.tmp files \u2014 no Python change needed\\n- The 3-step staging pattern fits naturally as an expansion of the existing WriteFile/UpdateEntry/FixIssues terminal nodes\\n\\nDIVERGENCE NOTE: There is a conflict between the groomed Desired Structure (.md.tmp naming, single-file staging) and the ungroomed Story/Target State section (uuid-based .research-curator-txn/ directory, --recover subcommand in validator). The groomed sections (Expected Behavior, Desired Structure, Acceptance Criteria) take precedence per grooming workflow scope boundary. If the uuid-txn approach is intended, the groomed Acceptance Criteria and Desired Structure must be updated before implementation begins.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` lines 354-388 \u2014 post_actions block documents `git add ./research/` directly; may need a note on .tmp file exclusion from git staging if `.gitignore` is updated\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nWrite pattern (atomic write via temp file + rename):\\n1. Write full content to {target}.md.tmp (same directory as target \u2014 ensures same filesystem).\\n2. Verify the temp file was written (size check or read-back).\\n3. Rename/move {target}.md.tmp to {target} \u2014 atomic on POSIX (os.replace() / rename(2)).\\n4. On error before step 3, delete {target}.md.tmp if it exists; propagate the error.\\n\\nTemp file naming: {name}.md.tmp suffix. Excluded from collect_files() because rglob(\\\"*.md\\\") does not match .md.tmp \u2014 verified from validate_research.py lines 363-365.\\n\\nPOSIX atomicity: rename(2) is atomic within the same filesystem. Temp and target share the same ./research/{category}/ directory \u2014 cross-filesystem rename is not a concern.\\n\\nNo new Python script required: The staging pattern is implemented via agent behavior (Claude Code Write tool + Bash rename, or Python pathlib.Path.replace() inline).\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The system permits a write operation that can be interrupted mid-way, leaving a partially-written file at the final path. No gate exists to prevent this outcome. The fix adds a safeguard (staging + atomic rename) that the system should have had from the start. There is no traceable defect chain \u2014 this is an absent protection mechanism, not a bug in existing logic.\\n**Analysis Method**: No analysis (missing-guardrail type \u2014 no 5-whys or 6-sigma required)\\n**Scenario Target**: research-curator mid-write interruption \u2192 partial entry file on disk \u2192 fix: write-to-temp-then-rename staging at all three write nodes\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an orchestrator running research-curator in batch or rerun mode, I want each research entry file write to be atomic so that an interruption mid-write leaves the previous valid entry intact \u2014 not a partially-written file that looks like a valid entry but fails content validation or contains truncated data.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` \u2014 primary write executor; contains all three write nodes\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` \u2014 orchestrator; no direct file writes; post-actions commits output\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` \u2014 validator; collect_files() uses rglob(\\\"*.md\\\") which excludes .md.tmp files; no code change needed\\n- `./research/` directory \u2014 output destination; no structural changes needed\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThe research-curator skill rewrites entries (`--rerun`, `--validate --fix`, default mode) and updates `./research/README.md` via direct Write/Edit calls. There is no transactional staging directory and no recovery helper. If a rewrite fails partway (process crash, disk-full, OOM kill, network drop while a sub-agent holds the file open), the entry on disk is left in a partial state with no rollback mechanism. Grep of `.claude/skills/research-curator/` for `txn`, `staging`, `rollback`, or `transactional` returns zero matches. Same gap exists for `validate_research.py --fix` runs that mutate multiple entries in sequence.\\n\\nFile: `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` (post-actions section, lines 354-388 \u2014 direct git stage and commit with no pre-write staging); `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThe research-curator skill rewrites entries (`--rerun`, `--validate --fix`, default mode) and updates `./research/README.md` via direct Write/Edit calls. There is no transactional staging directory and no recovery helper. If a rewrite fails partway (process crash, disk-full, OOM kill, network drop while a sub-agent holds the file open), the entry on disk is left in a partial state with no rollback mechanism. Grep of `.claude/skills/research-curator/` for `txn`, `staging`, `rollback`, or `transactional` returns zero matches. Same gap exists for `validate_research.py --fix` runs that mutate multiple entries in sequence.\\n\\nFile: `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` (post-actions section, lines 354-388 \u2014 direct git stage and commit with no pre-write staging); `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch-curator rewrites stage to `./research/.research-curator-txn/<uuid>/` first, then atomic-rename onto the target path on success. On startup (and on `--validate` invocation), the orchestrator scans for orphaned `.research-curator-txn/*` directories and either completes or rolls back each (configurable via flag). Failure mid-write leaves the original file untouched.\\n\\nField `staging_dir` exposed as `./research/.research-curator-txn/` in SKILL.md. The validator script has a new `--recover` subcommand that enumerates orphaned transactions and reports whether each is recoverable.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py --recover ./research/`. Output lists zero orphaned transactions on a clean tree. Inject a partial transaction (`mkdir ./research/.research-curator-txn/test-uuid; echo partial > ./research/.research-curator-txn/test-uuid/cocoindex-code.md`) and run the same command \u2014 it reports the orphan and recovers or removes it. Grep of `.claude/skills/research-curator/` for `staging_dir` or `txn` returns at least one match in SKILL.md and one in validate_research.py.\\n\\nSource: Tolaria research entry (./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md), Patterns Worth Adopting #3 \u2014 \\\"Crash-Safe File Operations: Use transactional staging directories (.tolaria-rename-txn/) and recovery helpers to ensure file operations complete or roll back cleanly.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"53448edb237eed46f2edb4c7e149f2b8cc9609f4e66356602a449fbf71f743f4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCUhkA\"}"}